       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is about double the maximum daily dose of 3200 mg/day in the labeling. The usual inpatient range is 400-800 mg per dose, up to 3200 mg/day.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 400-600 mg PO q6-8h** (common analgesic range)\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO q8h or 1600 mg PO BID**, if you intended 1600 mg per dose with a longer interval (4800 mg/day or less). Please confirm this is within your intent, since this is still a high total dose.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, I don't see other factors that change the dosing. Please also check for other NSAIDs or anticoagulants on the medication list, and for any GI bleeding risk."
      }
